{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485858-question-about-how-the-jam-weapon-gift-works","id":1485858,"title":"Question about how the Jam Weapon gift works","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-05T13:16:55-07:00","id":1485858,"title":"Question about how the Jam Weapon gift works","content":"I've got a question about how Jam Weapon should work in W20, because of an interesting situation that seems to pit rules as written against rules as intended. Here's the situation. A garou wants to use Jam Weapon against a bunch of enemies with rifles ready, about to fire on his pack. One of his packmates carries a dagger and has 9 dots of Willpower. Does the garou who wants to activate Jam Weapon always have to roll against a difficulty of 9, which his packmate's willpower, even if the packmate's dagger is dedicated and put away, for the gift to activate and jam the enemies' weapons? As written, the rule seems to punish the user for having strong packmates. I doubt that's the intent of the rule, but what do y'all think? Is there a simple way to solve this odd result of the rule that doesn't violate the intent of the gift?<br /> <br /> Also, and this may be a stupid question, but does the gift affect weapons that are carried by deaf people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T16:13:04-07:00","id":1485863,"title":"","content":"My initial instinct is to say that it should work like that. Jam Weapon is a level one tribal Gift for the Children of Gaia who are supposed to abhor violence and weapons. It makes sense one of their Gifts would indiscriminately nullify all weapons. The example of the spirit teaching the Gift is a dove spirit which means it is a peace spirit. I think the purpose of the Gift is to make everyone's weapons not work so that the Child of Gaia can calm down the situation, or allow one or more parties to leave the area safely. It's not meant to provide one side a combat advantage over another.<br /> <br /> That's my initial take. Could change my mind as I read the arguments of others.<br /> <br /> And I would rule that the Gift works even with people who are deaf. The Gift really isn't affecting them, but the weapons in their possession. It's just that the items themselves don't have Willpower. I guess the idea is that a tool in the hands of someone has their Willpower by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fixed typo 07-06-2022, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T10:09:02-07:00","id":1485912,"title":"","content":"Having read the Gift, I have to agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T11:54:46-07:00","id":1485926,"title":"","content":"While I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> on the interpretation of the intention, I'd add one option for this Gift: ignore the WP of anyone who just accepts the effect. That way, strong willed pack-mates may accept the effect to not hinder your efforts, still within the intention of the Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T13:38:34-07:00","id":1485937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485858-question-about-how-the-jam-weapon-gift-works?p=1485926#post1485926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> on the interpretation of the intention, I'd add one option for this Gift: ignore the WP of anyone who just accepts the effect. That way, strong willed pack-mates may accept the effect to not hinder your efforts, still within the intention of the Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I like that!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T11:55:35-07:00","id":1486165,"title":"","content":"I think most people will intuitively look past an ally holding a knife contributing their WP to the difficulty - but yeah if you think about it, people who accept peace shouldn't be opposing the effect difficulty wise.<br /> <br /> Also I'm playing a CoG for the first time and Jesus Christ does this Gift slap in crossover play. Nuh-Uh a HIT Mark for several turns. Only Brawl-based people are immune, and the Gift doesn't even break if you engage in hand-to-hand violence!<br /> <br /> Essentially you can turn off all of the Etherite steampunk flamethrowers and Verbenae superknives in the vicinity while your good old Gaia-given claws work great. Which feels like it runs a BIT against theme, but even the pacifists among warriors are still warriors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:42:04-07:00","id":1486175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> just to be clear, I don't think a HIT Mark counts as a weapon. It is a complex machine that <i>has</i> weapons, but that's a very different story. Given their general capabilities to carry out other purposes, I'd say their weapons may be jammed, but the robots themselves, not.<br /> <br /> And even from the perspective of a pacifist, hand-to-hand combat has the advantage of being less lethal, and you can think about this Gift under that light: it doesn't just reduce the risk of violence, it <b>greatly</b> reduces the lethality of such violence. For a Werewolf, while your claws are still pretty lethal, with less weapons to deal with it is easier to forgo their use without greater concerns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T13:19:28-07:00","id":1486178,"title":"","content":"Oh yes to be clear I was referring to jamming all of the weapons it owns, not just turning off the machine outright. Some models are very dangerous to a Garou even without weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}